/vendor/

# A library's lock file binds nobody: Composer resolves a dependency's requirements against
# the consuming project, never against this file. Committing it would pin a development
# checkout to versions no install ever sees, and hide the one thing the ranges are for.
/composer.lock

# Local answers to the shipped `.dist` configs. Each tool prefers the undotted name, so a
# file here wins over the one in the package -- and survives the next generation, which
# replaces everything else.
/.php-cs-fixer.php
/phpstan.neon

.php-cs-fixer.cache
.phpunit.cache
